<title>USA: Medpartners, Inphynet Hart-Scott period ends.</title>
<headline>Medpartners, Inphynet Hart-Scott period ends.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>MedPartners Inc and InPhyNet Medical Management Inc  said Friday that the waiting period required under the Hart-Scott Rodino Anti Trust Improvement Act with respect to their pending merger, announced Jan 21, has been terminated.</p>
<p>The proposed merger is valued at $493 million, and would result in a company with $5.2 billion in revenue, making it the largest provider of full time hospital-based physician services, said MedPartners.</p>
</text>
